4.—(1) For 2016, the amount of contribution to be paid under section 9(1)(b) of the Act is —
(a)$200 for a non‑schooling member who is at least 7 years of age but below 13 years of age;
(b)$200 for a non‑schooling member who —
(i)is at least 13 years of age but below 15 years of age;
(ii)is receiving home‑schooling as described in paragraph 3(1)(b)(i) to (vi) of the Compulsory Education (Exemption) Order (Cap. 51, O 1); and
(iii)did not perform, in 2015, at the Primary School Leaving Examination and the National Education Quiz, at such level of educational achievement as the Director‑General of Education may determine;
(c)$200 for a non‑schooling member who —
(i)is at least 13 years of age but below 17 years of age;
(ii)does not attain 17 years of age at any time in 2016; and
(iii)is receiving primary education in a designated school; and
(d)$240 for a non‑schooling member not referred to in sub‑paragraph (b) or (c), who —
(i)is at least 13 years of age but below 17 years of age; and
(ii)does not attain 17 years of age at any time in 2016.
(2) In this paragraph —
“designated school”, “home‑schooling”, “National Education Quiz” and “Primary School Leaving Examination” have the same meanings as in the Compulsory Education (Exemption) Order;
“non‑schooling member” means a member of the Edusave Pupils Fund who is not schooling at any time during 2016.
